C++ core language
-----------------

The C++ core-language features of each standard, in the order of cppreference's compiler support pages, with their feature-test macros. Rows without a macro are features that matter to a back end. Rows cover the features the EDG front end implements; features it lacks (for example contracts and expansion statements) are not listed. A macro value is listed when the front end defines that value or a later one; values above the front end's maximum are not listed. Status is for the cpfe-cir front end plus the CIR back end on x86-64 Linux (Itanium ABI).

