C language
----------

The C language by standard. A row is Yes only when a program compiled by cpfe-cir runs correctly. Evidence is a CIR test or a C corpus test (tests/.edgy/filters/cir-c-corpus.txt) that is not listed as failing in imported.log; corpus tests run in the importer's default (GNU) mode, so -std and dg-options are not applied unless the file's //options: line sets them (the c99-\*, c11-\* and c23-\* tests do). A Failing test fails under CIR today because of the row's gap.

